  "finished_because": "Admitted evidence already establishes a coherent causal chain: a 09:10 redeploy of notification-worker explicitly reintroduced the 'poison-message' revision; at ~09:30 notification-worker began crashing with an unhandled deserialization exception (log at 2026-07-02T09:30:50Z) and a restart_count alert fired at 09:30:09; while the consumer was crashing/restarting the Service Bus active_message_count rose sharply from ~26 at 09:30 to ~5.2k by 09:35 and remained >5k through 10:00. That explains why order notifications were delayed (notification-worker unable to process order-placed messages) and why the Service Bus queue depth climbed and did not drain (consumer crash loop caused processing to stop and messages to accumulate). The components and flows affected are notification-worker (consumer) reading order-placed events on service-bus and the downstream email-provider (deliveries blocked); checkout remains on the synchronous path and was not blocked. The impacted time window begins with the consumer crash/alert at ~2026-07-02T09:30:00+00:00 and continued at least until 2026-07-02T10:00:00+00:00, with approximately 5.2k queued messages observed at 09:35–10:00. No further evidence call is needed to state this causal chain because the deployment note, crash logs, restart alert, and service-bus metrics together provide the decisive signals required by the objective."
